A||||7||Matt88||Hi Perf Coil and plug gap||||1||
Z||000000||Matt88||02-24-2001||12:38 PM||||I'm planning on replacing my old worn out plug wires and adding a high performance coil to my '88 2.8  Does anyone have experience with the Accel or any other coil that they would recommend.<P>Also, is changing the plug gap (with the new coil) recommended?  It would seem with more volts and amps a larger gap would be beneficial.<P>It's a big enough pain to change the front plugs, I'd like to do it right the first time!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||PatrickB||02-24-2001||01:02 PM||||Im my opinion and experience, accel is no good and burn out quick.  I have an MSD which  has never been a problem and haven't heard as many bad things.<P><BR>Pat||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||02-24-2001||02:27 PM||||Ive had the Accel replacement for 2 years with no probs, 3.1 Turbo. As far as plugs I use Bosch Platinum, no gap to set.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||02-24-2001||04:18 PM||||Yeah I would recommend MSD over Accel anyday of the week.  Too many Accel products have left me stranded to ever trust them.  MSD is cheaper too.  Get a 6AL box too, for the gas mileage if anything (mine increased 5 mpg).<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">               <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">               <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||gixxer||02-24-2001||05:27 PM||||Put a MSD 6Al box and MSD coil on my normally aspirated 2.8, plugs gapped at .055". When I dropped the turbo in, I gapped the colder plugs at .040".<BR>If I just had the MSD coil on a stock engine, I might be tempted to gap it at about .050'. Be sure the plug wires and cap, etc. are up to snuff when running wider gaps. <BR>Wider the plug gap the better, assuming there are no high RPM misfires. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Matt88||02-24-2001||07:43 PM||||Thanks for the replies.  <P>I plan on replacing the plugs and wires (8mm) this month with a new coil next month (I've already replaced the cap and rotor).  <P>I think I'll gap the plugs at .050.  In anticipation of the new coil.  It's such a pain to take out the front plugs; I'll put up with some misfire in the meantime.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Sleeper||02-25-2001||11:30 AM||||damn, its pretty i ironic that i just read this post cuz my accel coil is starting to buzz and the last time it did that i had to replace it. my friends always told me not to get accel, geez. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||02-25-2001||11:37 AM||||well maybe if my Accel coil ever croaks on me ill try MSD, but its been working fine clear up to 7,000 RPM. I do know that Accel plugs and wires suck. Thats from experience.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
